{
  "id": "north-america-international-championships",
  "name": "North America International Championships",
  "category": "event",
  "description": {
    "text": "The North America International Championships are one of the International Championships that Play! Pokémon has held since the 2017 season, alongside Europe, Latin America and Oceania. Each International Championships promo came as a plain copy for every competitor, a Staff copy, and Top 8 and Champion copies for the players who reached the top eight of each division and for each division's winner.\n\nThe first, at the Indiana Convention Center in Indianapolis from 30 June to 2 July 2017, gave out Evolutions' Double Colorless Energy. Sun & Moon's Ultra Ball followed in 2018, the alternate-art Guardians Rising Choice Band numbered 121a in 2019, Fusion Strike's Quick Ball in 2022, Brilliant Stars' Ultra Ball in 2023, Scarlet & Violet's Nest Ball in 2024 and Temporal Forces' Buddy-Buddy Poffin in 2025, and Mega Evolution's Ultra Ball at the 2026 event in New Orleans on 12-14 June. From 2024 the event's logo sits on the card's picture.",
    "sources": [
